license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - computer algebra
  - symbolic computation
  - Julia
  - Giac
  - benchmark
abstract: >-
  Benches of computer algebra systems: Julia packages (Giac.jl, Symbolics.jl,
  SymJ.jl, Groebner.jl, Primes.jl, LibPARI.jl, msolve through
  AlgebraicSolving.jl), SymPy, and Maxima, FriCAS, SageMath and Macaulay2
  driven as processes: FFI overhead, CAS operations, integer factorisation,
  functional coverage, a 107-problem suite, a sample of the 12000.org
  integration tests, Gröbner bases and the OpenSymbolicRules integration
  rules. Fixed inputs, one adapter per system, every answer checked by a
  system-neutral test, every run dated and its environment pinned. The
  reproduced numbers of the JuliaCon Proceedings paper on Giac.jl.
